WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.235
-You guys, we're coming up
on a full year

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:04.237
since the COVID pandemic

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:06.405
radically changed
all of our lives,

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:07.740
and even though we just passed

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.076
the devastating milestone
of half a million deaths,

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:14.280
there are now finally some real
glimmers of hope on the horizon.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.949
For more on this,
it's time for a Closer Look.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:20.653 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.088
There's one question that
everyone's been asking every day

00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:24.991
to friends, neighbors,
relatives, and that is,

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:27.627
"When will everything
get back to normal?"

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.395
We're all itching to
do normal things again.

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:30.629
It doesn't matter what it is.

00:00:30.629 --> 00:00:32.998
I'd give anything to go wait
in line at the DMV

00:00:32.998 --> 00:00:35.835
and get yelled at by a clerk
for asking to borrow a pen.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:39.071
I want to squeeze avocados
at Trader Joe's without

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:41.074
people looking me up and down
for signs of fever.

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:43.642
Keep your eyes
on your own avocados!

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:45.010
And yet,
predictions for normalcy

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.312
have been all over the map

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.015
from as early as April
to as late as next year.

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:51.183 line:0%
-In a "Wall Street Journal"
opinion piece,

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:54.253 line:0%
Johns Hopkins health expert
Marty Makary

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:56.856 line:0%
claims we're going to
have herd immunity by April.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.292 line:0%
-I think we could get there
by the fall,

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.194 line:0%
or maybe even
by the end of the summer.

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:03.062 line:0%
-The Institute for Health
Metrics and Evaluation

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:05.197 line:0%
at the University of Washington
says it does not expect

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:08.267 line:0%
the US to reach herd immunity
prior to next winter.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:10.536 line:0%
-By next Christmas,

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:12.972 line:0%
I think we'll be in
a very different circumstance,

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:15.675 line:0%
God willing, than we are today.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.744 line:0%
-You and the president
have suggested

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.946 line:0%
that we'll approach normality
toward the end of the year.

00:01:20.946 --> 00:01:22.348 line:0%
What does "normal" mean?

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.850 line:0%
Do you think Americans
will still be wearing masks,

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:28.521 line:0%
for example, in 2022?

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:31.457 line:0%
-You know, I think it is
possible that that's the case.

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:33.425 line:0%
-We are not in a place
where we can predict

00:01:33.425 --> 00:01:35.561 line:0%
exactly when everybody
will feel normal again.

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:37.897 line:0%
-Dinner and a movie in New York
could be around the corner.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:40.266 line:0%
The movie theaters are open
with reduced capacity.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:41.234 line:0%
Indoor dining.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.268 line:0%
Will we get back to normal?

00:01:43.268 --> 00:01:44.203 line:0%
-I'm staying outside.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:45.571 line:0%
-Yeah, me too, actually.

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:47.873
-Oh, thanks for the tease, CNN.

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:49.575
Dinner and a movie
is back in the Big Apple,

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:50.576
but not for us.

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:51.810
We're not ready to die.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.812
Enjoy your Brussels sprouts
and "Tom &amp; Jerry,"

00:01:53.812 --> 00:01:55.848
you suicidal maniacs.

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:57.583
In fairness, though,
that's how we all feel.

00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.686
Everyone has had
that same conversation

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:02.521
whenever they ease restrictions
on something, on anything.

00:02:02.521 --> 00:02:05.290
"Wow, they're reopening
bowling alleys. Amazing.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:06.726
We should take the kids."

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:09.729
"Yeah, but not really, right?

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:10.930
And wear community shoes

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.364
and stick our fingers
in a bunch of dark holes?

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:13.799
No, of course not."

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:16.669
Problem is, no one knows for
certain when it'll be safe,

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:18.504
and we can't know for certain.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:19.672
As you just heard,

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.274
predictions for when
we'll return to normal

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.342
range from April
to summer to fall

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:24.543
to Christmas to next year.

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:25.845
At this rate, I'm just hoping

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:30.015
to have an audience back
for my farewell show.

00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:32.685
I'm back in a suit?

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.353
So the first show they're back,

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:36.088
you're going to put me
in a [bleep] suit.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:38.991
[Bleep] you, Shoemaker.

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:43.896
I don't dance for you.

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:45.297
And look, caution is good.

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:47.200
We can't underestimate
this virus.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.667
It's been devastating,
and every time

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.203
we think the worst is behind us,
it comes roaring back.

00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:53.705
It's like the McRib
but with a switchblade.

00:02:53.705 --> 00:02:55.808
We have to keep our foot
on the gas

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:57.176
and stamp
this thing out for good.

00:02:57.176 --> 00:03:00.446
But there's also some
genuinely, genuinely good news,

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.682
setting the stage for
what "The Atlantic" called

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.550
"A quite possibly
wonderful summer."

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:07.153
And look, I know
I've spent the past year

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:09.355
starting each of these segments
by rattling off

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.491
all the worst things
going on in the world,

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:14.493
like a grandpa who immediately
launches into a laundry list

00:03:14.493 --> 00:03:16.262
of his medical issues
when you call him.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.730
"How are you, Grandpa?"

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.533
"Well, my sciatica's back
and my winter skin won't go away

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.101
and my blood pressure's
through the roof

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.903
and I can't find
my hernia pillow."

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.338
"Well, what about grandma?"

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:30.509
"Hold on a sec. Barb? Barb?

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:32.345
The boy wants
to know how you are.

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:36.549
No, it's not a scam call,
you paranoid lunatic.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:40.553
She's fine. She's the same."

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.087
So let's start, for a change,

00:03:42.087 --> 00:03:43.489
by reviewing
some of the good news.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.757
Today,
the FDA confirmed that

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.692
Johnson &amp; Johnson's
new one-shot vaccine

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:49.362
is safe and effective,
especially against severe cases.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:50.630
Pfizer said this week it will

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.965
double its weekly
shipments by mid-March.

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:55.100
Pfizer and Moderna
told lawmakers they can

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.636
dramatically increase deliveries
over the next five weeks,

00:03:57.636 --> 00:03:59.572
and between those
three vaccines,

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:02.675
we could have a total
of 240 million doses

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.410
by the end of March alone.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.178
All of which means
there's growing optimism

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:08.214
about the course of
the coronavirus pandemic

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:11.050
and the possible return to some
semblance of normalcy by summer.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.453
And I got to be honest, I
desperately need some optimism.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:15.320
They don't teach you this
in science class,

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:18.157
but it turns out winter
during a pandemic [bleep] sucks.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.626
It's like my soul
has a hangnail.

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:22.127
The sun goes down at 5:00.

00:04:22.127 --> 00:04:25.965
I'm wearing a whole outfit made
of SNL swag from 15 years ago,

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:29.068
watching 20 minutes
of some Belgian Netflix drama

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.703
before I realize
I watched it already.

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:34.573
"Wait, Detective Bert Jansens?
[Bleep]. I've seen this.

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:39.544
The body's in the canal,
Jansens!

00:04:39.544 --> 00:04:41.113
It's always in the canal.

00:04:41.113 --> 00:04:43.982
I don't know why
you didn't start there."

00:04:43.982 --> 00:04:45.150
Last week, I told my wife

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:46.819
I was gonna regrout
the tile in the bathroom

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.220
just to have something to do,

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.789
but then she pointed out we
don't have tile in the bathroom,

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:52.959
so I installed
tile in the bathroom

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:54.260
just so I could regrout it.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.828
Also, I did a bad job
installing it,

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.330
so we had to bring in a guy who
I'm certain is ripping me off.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:01.734
I mean, $1,000 per tile
is too much, right?

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.902
So it's helpful to remember
there is some good news.

00:05:03.902 --> 00:05:05.438
Cases are falling
as dramatically

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:06.572
as they've ever fallen,

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.741
and vaccine supply
is ramping up quickly,

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:10.276
thanks in part
to the Biden administration

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:11.810
delivering more doses
to the states.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:14.847
In fact, both Democratic
and Republican governors

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:16.248
have praised the Biden
administration

00:05:16.248 --> 00:05:17.617
for streamlining what was,

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:20.486
before he took office,
a chaotic vaccine rollout.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.988 line:0%
-The White House
press secretary, Jen Psaki,

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:23.055 line:0%
announcing just moments ago

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:24.957 line:0%
the Biden administration
now increasing

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:27.893 line:0%
its weekly COVID-19
vaccine supplies to states,

00:05:27.893 --> 00:05:30.696 line:0%
upping it now to
13.5 million doses

00:05:30.696 --> 00:05:33.032 line:0%
sent out to the states
on a weekly basis.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.700 line:0%
-The Biden team
is doing a great job.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.769 line:0%
They inherited
an empty cupboard.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:40.339 line:0%
They're slowly but surely
fixing that.

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:43.442 line:0%
-In terms of
the vaccine distribution,

00:05:43.442 --> 00:05:46.412 line:0%
it's been seamless, and
I was delighted that we had

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:52.184 line:0%
a 14 percent increase
in vaccine supply last week.

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:54.887 line:0%
This is going to be very,
very important for us.

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.855 line:0%
Thank goodness we have
that partnership

00:05:56.855 --> 00:05:59.725 line:0%
which is good with
the federal government

00:05:59.725 --> 00:06:01.394 line:0%
and President Biden and his team

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:04.863 line:0%
is working to assure
that partnership

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:08.167 line:0%
and not tear it apart,
which I'm very grateful for.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:11.503
Huh, so it turns out
you can just buy more

00:06:11.503 --> 00:06:14.773
of a life-saving vaccine
and give more of it out,

00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:16.241
and both Republicans
and Democrats

00:06:16.241 --> 00:06:17.376
will thank you for it?

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:19.378
I'm no political genius,
but that seems like

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:21.480
a slightly better strategy than,
I don't know,

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.549
personally trying to
spread the disease

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:26.652
to as many people as you can,
like President Outbreak Monkey.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:30.456
Sorry, Former President
Outbreak Monkey.

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:31.591
I mean, there were times

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.126
when Democratic governors
praised Trump,

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:35.294
but it was with the dead eyes
of a hostage who is worried

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:36.962
they'd have their
bathroom privileges revoked,

00:06:36.962 --> 00:06:39.198
whereas if Republicans
criticize Biden,

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:41.233
their fear isn't that
he'll punish them,

00:06:41.233 --> 00:06:43.035
it's that he will show up
to the governor's mansion

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:44.369
with a football and say,

00:06:44.369 --> 00:06:46.939
"You and I are going to
toss this pigskin back and forth

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:48.608
until we find
some middle ground."

00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:50.943
"Oh, actually, Mr. President,
I was just about to go out."

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:52.912
"You're damn right you're
going out. Down and out.

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:55.914
Hut! Hut! Everyone's my friend."

00:06:55.914 --> 00:06:58.518
By the way, none of this means
Biden hasn't made some mistakes

00:06:58.518 --> 00:07:00.553
or that there haven't been
disappointments

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:01.621
with some of his early moves.

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:02.821
There have.

00:07:02.821 --> 00:07:04.322
For one thing,
he seems resigned to dropping

00:07:04.322 --> 00:07:06.692
a minimum wage increase
from the COVID relief plan,

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:09.027
despite its overwhelming
popularity in the polls

00:07:09.027 --> 00:07:11.230
and strong support
from Senate Democrats

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:13.032
like Chuck Schumer
and Bernie Sanders.

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:16.035
He's flirted with narrowing the
eligibility for direct payments,

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:17.370
and he's shot down proposals

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.605
to cancel
$50,000 in student debt,

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:22.475
which also has
majority support in polls

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:24.510
and would be a huge boon
to the economy.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:26.545 line:0%
-We need student loan
forgiveness beyond

00:07:26.545 --> 00:07:30.115 line:0%
the potential $10,000 your
administration has proposed.

00:07:30.115 --> 00:07:33.519 line:0%
We need at least
a $50,000 minimum.

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:35.287 line:0%
What will you do
to make that happen?

00:07:35.287 --> 00:07:37.256 line:0%
-I will not make that happen.

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:40.392
-Okay, enough of your
Washington Beltway double-speak.

00:07:40.392 --> 00:07:41.994
Are you going to make it
happen or not?

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:43.963 line:0%
-I will not make that happen.

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:47.233
-Oh, you DC charlatans, always
trying to have it both ways.

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:48.334
Are you going to make it happen?

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:50.569 line:0%
-I will not make that happen.

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:52.772
-Damn, that is not the answer
I wanted to hear,

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.873
but I do appreciate
his directness.

00:07:54.873 --> 00:07:56.141
The last guy answered questions

00:07:56.141 --> 00:07:59.144
the way a plane circles JFK
when it's foggy.

00:07:59.144 --> 00:08:00.479
Say what you will about Biden,

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:02.848
but in many ways, he is
the exact opposite of Trump.

00:08:02.848 --> 00:08:04.750
A reporter at a press conference
could raise their hand

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.085
and suggest literally anything

00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:07.819
and Trump would say
he was considering it.

00:08:07.819 --> 00:08:09.588
It's the only reason
you could never trick him.

00:08:09.588 --> 00:08:11.323
Mr. President,
do you have any response

00:08:11.323 --> 00:08:13.626
to the recent events
regarding Updog?

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:16.328
"We're looking very,
very strongly at Updog.

00:08:16.328 --> 00:08:18.697
We don't like what they're
doing with Updog at all.

00:08:18.697 --> 00:08:20.533
It's not good.

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:23.268
Oh, I much prefer Downdog,
don't we, folks?

00:08:23.268 --> 00:08:27.106
Or how about just good,
old-fashioned, regular dog?

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:30.076
Whatever happened to dogs
without directions?

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:31.777
There used to be
no such thing as Updog.

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:33.746
No Downdog.

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:37.983
No, Rightdog. No Leftdog.
There was just dog.

00:08:37.983 --> 00:08:40.086
Dog the Bounty Hunter.

00:08:40.086 --> 00:08:44.890
Bounty paper towels,
the quicker picker-upper,

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:45.924
they like to say.

00:08:45.924 --> 00:08:47.826
A lot of people
are saying it now.

00:08:47.826 --> 00:08:51.230
Not as quick as it used to be.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:53.332
Sad.

00:08:53.332 --> 00:08:58.337
Tried to pick it up lately,
and it wasn't so quick at all.

00:08:58.337 --> 00:08:59.438
Slow."

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:08.314
I both forgot how hard
it was to do that voice,

00:09:08.314 --> 00:09:11.016
and how it was little bit fun.

00:09:11.016 --> 00:09:13.218
I'm definitely going to have
to ice my voice tonight.

00:09:13.218 --> 00:09:15.254
Oh.

00:09:15.254 --> 00:09:16.988
Anyway, the point is,
the Biden administration

00:09:16.988 --> 00:09:19.325
has certainly had some missteps
and disappointments,

00:09:19.325 --> 00:09:21.360
but they've also been
bold out of the gate

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.596
with executive actions
and their COVID relief plan,

00:09:23.596 --> 00:09:25.697
and there's been major progress
on the vaccine front.

00:09:25.697 --> 00:09:27.199
The rollout
has been streamlined.

00:09:27.199 --> 00:09:29.568
Supply is up,
and the news about

00:09:29.568 --> 00:09:31.803
just how effective the vaccines
are has been great, too.

00:09:31.803 --> 00:09:35.374
A new study has found that just
one dose of the Pfizer vaccine

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:37.576
provides significant protection
against the infection,

00:09:37.576 --> 00:09:39.378
and another found
that the vaccines

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:41.513
cut down on transmission, too,

00:09:41.513 --> 00:09:44.684
meaning the vaccines don't just
prevent you from getting sick,

00:09:44.684 --> 00:09:46.818
they prevent you
from spreading the virus, too.

00:09:46.818 --> 00:09:49.455
If that all ends up being true,
and we don't screw things up,

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:51.323
we could potentially
have a normal-ish summer,

00:09:51.323 --> 00:09:53.825
Even typically cautious
public health officials

00:09:53.825 --> 00:09:55.394
are expressing optimism.

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:58.964 line:0%
-Essentially, what will happen
is it's a glide path down.

00:09:58.964 --> 00:10:01.433 line:0%
Number of cases
will continue coming down.

00:10:01.433 --> 00:10:03.469 line:0%
More and more people will
be getting vaccinated.

00:10:03.469 --> 00:10:05.237 line:0%
Things will start opening up.

00:10:05.237 --> 00:10:07.740 line:0%
We'll see occasional
outbreaks here and there.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.608 line:0%
I'm expecting, and I've
been saying it to folks,

00:10:09.608 --> 00:10:10.876 line:0%
and you're invited, John,

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:13.746 line:0%
that July 4th, I may have
a barbecue at my house.

00:10:13.746 --> 00:10:17.082 line:0%
20-25 people, and I think
we can be outside

00:10:17.082 --> 00:10:19.885 line:0%
if everybody
shows up vaccinated

00:10:19.885 --> 00:10:21.887 line:0%
and if everybody's
gotten vaccinated

00:10:21.887 --> 00:10:23.489 line:0%
or most people have gotten
vaccinated in my community,

00:10:23.489 --> 00:10:26.124 line:0%
which I suspect by July 4th,
they will.

00:10:26.124 --> 00:10:28.126 line:0%
I think we can have
an outside barbecue,

00:10:28.126 --> 00:10:30.429 line:0%
no masks, and be okay.

00:10:30.429 --> 00:10:32.865
-Damn, I didn't realize
it was at the point

00:10:32.865 --> 00:10:34.366
where someone
describing a barbecue

00:10:34.366 --> 00:10:35.834
would sound like erotica.

00:10:35.834 --> 00:10:38.570
You could sell a whole line
of romance novels on this vibe.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:41.840
I got chills thinking about
a barbecue with 25 friends,

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:44.242
and then I immediately got sad
when I remembered I'm 47

00:10:44.242 --> 00:10:45.911
and I definitely
don't have 25 friends.

00:10:45.911 --> 00:10:47.747
For me to have a party
with 25 friends,

00:10:47.747 --> 00:10:51.016
I'm going to need the vaccine
and a working time machine.

00:10:51.016 --> 00:10:52.351
Get on it, Pfizer.

00:10:52.351 --> 00:10:54.419
But honestly though,
I can't believe how excited I am

00:10:54.419 --> 00:10:55.754
at the prospect of making plans

00:10:55.754 --> 00:10:58.023
Before the pandemic,
I spent most of my time

00:10:58.023 --> 00:10:59.758
trying to get out of plans.

00:10:59.758 --> 00:11:01.793
Pre-pandemic,
the highlight of my week

00:11:01.793 --> 00:11:03.762
would be a friend
texting last minute

00:11:03.762 --> 00:11:05.865
that they can't make
after-work drinks

00:11:05.865 --> 00:11:07.032
because their babysitter bailed.

00:11:07.032 --> 00:11:09.067
Now, if that ever happens,
post-pandemic,

00:11:09.067 --> 00:11:12.271
I'll show up at their house with
some gin, a cocktail shaker,

00:11:12.271 --> 00:11:14.573
and a board game
that takes eight hours to play.

00:11:14.573 --> 00:11:15.841
It's called "Ocean Master."

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:18.276
You score victory points
by mining precious minerals

00:11:18.276 --> 00:11:20.846
from deep-sea trenches,
which convert to gold coins,

00:11:20.846 --> 00:11:23.616
allowing you to buy islands
where you grow wheat,

00:11:23.616 --> 00:11:27.019
and whoever sells the most bread
gets to roll first.

00:11:27.019 --> 00:11:29.455
The directions are 500 pages
long and only in German.

00:11:29.455 --> 00:11:31.824
Now, this isn't to say things
can't change for the worse.

00:11:31.824 --> 00:11:33.825
If we loosen up too quickly
or not enough people

00:11:33.825 --> 00:11:35.594
get vaccinated
or the variants get worse,

00:11:35.594 --> 00:11:36.662
we could have setbacks.

00:11:36.662 --> 00:11:38.797
But the streamlined
vaccine rollout

00:11:38.797 --> 00:11:40.765
and the optimism from
public health officials

00:11:40.765 --> 00:11:43.135
are a nice change of pace

00:11:43.135 --> 00:11:44.436
after the previous
administration,

00:11:44.436 --> 00:11:46.405
which was so mendacious
and detached from reality,

00:11:46.405 --> 00:11:47.839
you couldn't trust
a word they said.

00:11:47.839 --> 00:11:50.175
Remember when Trump's
chief of staff, Mark Meadows,

00:11:50.175 --> 00:11:53.011
said this last year
in the run-up to the election?

00:11:53.011 --> 00:11:57.149
-Our goal has been to have
300 million doses by January.

00:11:57.149 --> 00:11:59.651
100 million doses is
one-third of the population.

00:11:59.651 --> 00:12:02.688
That's pretty wide distribution,
when you look at that,

00:12:02.688 --> 00:12:03.755
and that's October.

00:12:03.755 --> 00:12:05.891
-They said we'd have
100 million doses

00:12:05.891 --> 00:12:09.961
by the end of October
and 300 million by January.

00:12:09.961 --> 00:12:12.164
Trump aides were less
trustworthy than those robots

00:12:12.164 --> 00:12:14.299
that call you about
your car's extended warranty,

00:12:14.299 --> 00:12:16.635
a call I get every damn day,
by the way.

00:12:16.635 --> 00:12:18.203
Side note,
what's going on with that?

00:12:18.203 --> 00:12:20.072
Who unleashed this army
of robot scammers

00:12:20.072 --> 00:12:22.241
trying to trick people into
buying extended car warranties?

00:12:22.241 --> 00:12:24.810
Are there really people out
there who fall for that?

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:26.211
"Oh, good thing you called.

00:12:26.211 --> 00:12:29.081
I was worried about the warranty
on my 2003 Ford Fiesta.

00:12:29.081 --> 00:12:32.050
You have a strange voice. Are
you French? Ooh, are you German?

00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:34.486
If you are, can I read you
board game instructions?

00:12:34.486 --> 00:12:38.190
[ Speaking in German ]

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:39.825
Seriously, I knew
the Trump people were liars,

00:12:39.825 --> 00:12:42.294
but it's even more brazen in
retrospect, especially compared

00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:44.262
to the overly cautious approach
of the Biden team.

00:12:44.262 --> 00:12:45.697
I mean, Biden's out here saying

00:12:45.697 --> 00:12:47.566
we won't get back
to normal until Christmas.

00:12:47.566 --> 00:12:49.768
He's going to miss the barbecue.

00:12:49.768 --> 00:12:51.670
Meanwhile, the Trump people were
going around telling everyone

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.672
we'd all get vaccines
in the mail for Christmas,

00:12:53.672 --> 00:12:56.108
like they were
free AOL trial CDs.

00:12:56.108 --> 00:12:58.076
As we've said
many times on this show,

00:12:58.076 --> 00:13:00.312
things are still bad
for lots of people

00:13:00.312 --> 00:13:02.881
who need immediate help
in the form of direct payments,

00:13:02.881 --> 00:13:05.817
expanded unemployment benefits,
a $15 minimum wage,

00:13:05.817 --> 00:13:07.619
and a more robust
vaccine rollout

00:13:07.619 --> 00:13:10.322
in marginalized communities,
among other things.

00:13:10.322 --> 00:13:11.756
And the pandemic
has also exposed

00:13:11.756 --> 00:13:13.391
massive structural inequalities

00:13:13.391 --> 00:13:15.193
and problems that need
radical solutions.

00:13:15.193 --> 00:13:16.462
We can't let up now.

00:13:16.462 --> 00:13:17.729
The next few months
will be crucial,

00:13:17.729 --> 00:13:20.633
but there's finally
some reason for hope

00:13:20.633 --> 00:13:22.000
and some cautious optimism.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:24.303
We could even have a party
at my place this summer.

00:13:24.303 --> 00:13:25.303
What do you say?

00:13:25.303 --> 00:13:26.605 line:0%
-I'm staying outside?

00:13:26.605 --> 00:13:27.740 line:0%
-Yeah, me too, actually.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.642
-Okay, fine, fine.

00:13:29.642 --> 00:13:31.109
This has been a Closer Look.

00:13:31.109 --> 00:13:34.479 line:0%
♪♪

00:13:34.479 --> 00:13:35.681
God's Love We Deliver

00:13:35.681 --> 00:13:37.482
cooks and brings over
2 million meals a year

00:13:37.482 --> 00:13:38.717
to men, women, and children
living with

00:13:38.717 --> 00:13:41.086
HIV, AIDS, cancer, and
other serious illnesses,

00:13:41.086 --> 00:13:42.654
and they need your help
now more than ever.

00:13:42.654 --> 00:13:44.856
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:13:44.856 --> 00:13:47.760
Stay safe. Wash your hands.
Wear a mask. We love you.

